From: OpenWrt JCOW414 build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feeds/packages: glib2 — assemble vendored libffi with MIPS16 disabled

glib2 2.88.x vendors libffi 3.5.2 whose mips/o32.S fails to assemble on
the mipsel_24kc target with:

    .cprestore not supported in MIPS16 mode
    invalid operands `move $fp,$sp` / `sw $4,offset($fp)`

The assembler enters MIPS16 mode for the hand-written .S and rejects
standard MIPS o32 mnemonics. Force the legacy encoding with
-mno-mips16 for the whole package (the .S is compiled through the
target C compiler, which inherits CFLAGS).

---
 a/feeds/packages/libs/glib2/Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
--- a/feeds/packages/libs/glib2/Makefile
+++ b/feeds/packages/libs/glib2/Makefile
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 PKG_CPE_ID:=cpe:/a:gnome:glib

 PKG_BUILD_DIR:=$(BUILD_DIR)/glib-$(PKG_VERSION)
+TARGET_CFLAGS += -mno-mips16
 PKG_CONFIG_DEPENDS:=CONFIG_BUILD_NLS
 PKG_FORTIFY_SOURCE:=0
 PKG_BUILD_FLAGS:=gc-sections
